  "id": "COMPOUND:26271 - PROTEIN:3743",
  "verbalization": "Chlorajapolide E is shown to interact with G1/S-specific cyclin-D1, a protein involved in the regulation of the cell cycle. This interaction is supported by multiple pathways, all of which lead to the target Fibrinogen beta chain. The evidence suggests that Chlorajapolide E may inhibit cyclin-D1, which in turn affects the function of Fibrinogen beta chain. The presence of multiple distinct molecular targets for cyclin-D1, including (3S,3aS,5aS,6S,9R,9aS,10aR)-5a,9,10a-trimethyl-3-prop-1-en-2-yl-2,3,3a,4,5,6,7,8,9a,10-decahydro-1H-benzo[f]azulene-6,9-diol and (2R,3S)-3-[(2S,3S)-5,7-dihydroxy-2-(4-methoxyphenyl)-4-oxo-2,3-dihydrochromen-3-yl]-5,7-dihydroxy-2-(4-hydroxyphenyl)-2,3-dihydrochromen-4-one, indicates that the compound may act through a broad mechanism that targets different isoforms of cyclin-D1. The shared pathway to Fibrinogen beta chain suggests that the inhibition of cyclin-D1 may have a downstream effect on the synthesis or function of fibrinogen, potentially through cellular signaling or metabolic pathways. The integrated evidence supports a mechanistic link between Chlorajapolide E and Fibrinogen beta chain, mediated by the regulation of cyclin-D1.",
